        "node_id": "n_1_2af678",
        "thought_text": "To solve the problem, we can first identify the unique elements in the given sequence and count their occurrences. We then calculate the number of ways to arrange these unique elements such that no element is sorted. This involves understanding the constraints imposed by the sorted definition and using combinatorial mathematics to count valid permutations.",
