        "node_id": "n_3_ee3323",
        "thought_text": "A third strategy involves leveraging graph theory. We can construct a graph where each node represents an element in the sequence, and edges represent the conditions under which elements cannot be sorted. By analyzing the connected components of this graph, we can determine the number of permutations that result in an entirely unsorted sequence.",
